set('twentyfour:1',find('eight:Junior-01').directAnswer,find('eight:Junior-01').explanation,'# Rails provides this web-specific DSL; it is not Ruby core.\nRails.application.routes.draw do\n  resources :articles\nend',['Rails supplies web conventions and ORM behavior; Ruby supplies the language.'],['Removed unsupported claims about “Mediterranean quality”, code rearrangement, and Rails introducing many-to-many relationships.']);
set('twentyfour:2','Save code in a .rb file and execute ruby filename.rb. Read script arguments from ARGV and interactive standard input from $stdin.','Use ruby -v to confirm the runtime and ruby -c file.rb to check syntax. Shell background syntax depends on the operating system: & has shell-specific behavior and is not a portable Ruby backgrounding API. The source’s Shell#open URL example is not a reliable browser-launching interface.','name = ARGV.first || $stdin.gets&.chomp || "guest"\nputs "Hello, #{name}"\n# ruby hello.rb Asha',['Handle EOF: gets may return nil.','Keep process execution and browser launching separate from Ruby script syntax.'],['Corrected nonportable backgrounding advice and unsupported require "shell"/Shell#open browser example.']);
set('twentyfour:5','A Ruby constant starts with an uppercase letter and is resolved through lexical and namespace rules. Reassignment is possible and usually warns; freezing its referenced value does not prevent rebinding.','Nested module definitions and A::B definitions have different lexical nesting. Use qualified names to make cross-namespace access explicit. ALL_CAPS is a convention for value constants; class/module names are constants too. Ruby has no ordinary language rule that makes every constant a global variable. Call warn or Warning.warn for messages; the source’s warning method is not a standard replacement.','module Geometry\n  RADIUS = 5.0\n  LABEL = "circle".freeze\nend\np Geometry::RADIUS\n# Geometry::LABEL = "new" reassigns the constant (with a warning).',['Reference: '+DOC+'syntax/modules_and_classes_rdoc.html'],['Corrected global-scope claim, unsupported warning invocation and claim that freeze prohibits constant reassignment.']);
set('twentyfour:6','require loads code; include mixes a module’s instance methods into a class or another module. These are different operations and neither replaces the other.','require may run wherever a library is needed and searches configured load paths; require_relative is useful for nearby files. include alters the receiver’s ancestry and works with modules, not arbitrary classes. First load the module definition if needed, then include it into the intended receiver.','require_relative "greetable"\nclass User\n  include Greetable\nend',['Repeated require normally skips an already loaded feature.']);
set('twentyfour:7',find('seven:12').directAnswer,find('seven:12').explanation+' String is not Enumerable, so use scan for extracting matches or each_line/each_char before Enumerable operations. Use numeric times/upto/step to express repetitions. Array#each returns its receiver, collect is an alias of map, and step advances values rather than indenting output.','text = "Email user@example.com"\np text.scan(/\\b[\\w.+-]+@[\\w.-]+\\.[A-Za-z]{2,}\\b/)\n1.upto(5) { |n| puts "*" * n }',['The sample regex is illustrative, not a full email-address validator.'],['Corrected String#grep misuse, each return-value claim, collect distinction, String#upto star output and “step indents” claim.']);
set('twentyfour:8','Handle expected exceptions with targeted rescue clauses, clean up with ensure and raise meaningful StandardError subclasses for recoverable application failures.','SystemCallError is itself a subclass of StandardError; these are not two disjoint top-level categories. A bare rescue catches StandardError descendants, not every Exception subclass. at_exit can observe termination and perform cleanup but is not a substitute for local recovery. Attempt the file read and handle the actual exception rather than relying only on a prior exists? check that can race.','def read_config(path)\n  File.read(path)\nrescue Errno::ENOENT => error\n  warn error.message\n  nil\nend',['A custom exception inheriting directly from Exception will not be caught by a bare rescue.'],['Corrected exception hierarchy, claim that every custom exception is rescued automatically, and check-before-read race.']);
set('twentyfour:9',find('seven:1').directAnswer,find('seven:1').explanation,find('seven:1').example,find('seven:1').importantPoints,['Corrected invalid naming regex, variable access-control claim, local lifetime claim (closures retain locals) and instance-variable external visibility.']);
addIssue('twentyfour:10','Source declares both attr_reader and attr_writer, so name=/age= assignments succeed; the comments claiming errors are wrong.');
set('twentyfour:11',find('seven:15').directAnswer,find('seven:15').explanation,find('seven:15').example,find('seven:15').importantPoints,['Removed unsupported Ruby 2.6 “trashcan” and context-dependent reference-counting/hybrid claims; count_objects[:FREE] is not a collector-enabling API.']);
set('twentyfour:12','chomp removes a record separator, normally one line ending; strip removes leading and trailing whitespace. Neither is interchangeable with the other.','gets can return nil at EOF. chomp preserves ordinary leading and trailing spaces, whereas strip removes them; passing a separator changes chomp’s behavior. Input cleaning is a domain decision, not general security validation.','line = "  Asha  \\n"\np line.chomp # "  Asha  "\np line.strip # "Asha"',['Use $stdin.gets&.chomp when EOF is allowed.','Reference: '+DOC+'String.html'],['Corrected false claim that chomp removes all trailing whitespace.']);
set('twentyfour:15',find('eight:Mid-01').directAnswer,'Use define_method for a known set of generated methods, public_send with an allowlist for selected public operations, and method_missing/respond_to_missing? for a genuinely open dynamic interface. Reopening String can overwrite existing behavior globally; prefer a dedicated helper or refinement. Never eval external input. The source’s instance-level visibility toggler calls a private method externally and attempts to use Module visibility APIs on an ordinary object; define visibility in the class/module context instead. Blindly sending a cleaned missing name can recurse forever if the cleaned method is also absent. Internationalization should normally select known translations rather than evaluate dynamically constructed code.',find('eight:Mid-01').example,['send bypasses private visibility; public_send is narrower but still needs an allowlist for external names.','method_missing is not required to implement duck typing.'],['Corrected nonworking visibility example, recursive method_missing risk, unsafe eval localization recommendation and overstatement that method_missing is the heart of duck typing.']);
